# React Component Contract

## File structure

Each component lives in its own `.tsx` file. Its CSS lives in a sibling `.css` file with the same base name.

## Props

- Props interface declared immediately above the component function, never exported unless reused elsewhere.
- All prop fields must be `readonly`: `type Props = { readonly onDismiss: () => void }` (linter rule S6759).
- Destructure all props in the function signature.
- Avoid spreading `...props` onto DOM elements.

## State

- Component-local state via `useState`. Shared cross-screen state (active packings list) is reloaded from IndexedDB on each screen mount — no global mutable store.

## Events

- Event handler props named `on<Action>`.
- Handler functions inside the component named `handle<Action>`.

## Rendering

- Each area of the UI has exactly one component responsible for rendering it.
- No component imperatively renders another's content.

## Accessibility

- Interactive elements use semantic HTML (`button`, `a`, `nav`, etc.).
- `aria-label` on icon-only buttons.
- All interactive items are reachable by keyboard.

## Mobile conventions

- Touch targets are at least 44×44 px.
- No hover-only interactions — all actions available via tap.
- Destructive actions (delete, discard) require a confirmation step.
